# Vulnerability details

## Impact

If the reward token in the pool is any token in the pool, then the `deposit` operation of the contract `Curve2PoolAdapter` will be recognized as `Swap`

## Proof of Concept

For users, Swap, Deposit, and Withdraw are all related to inputToken and outputToken.

```solidity
    function _determineComputeType(
        uint256 inputToken,
        uint256 outputToken
    )
        private
        view
        returns (ComputeType computeType)
    {
        if (((inputToken == xToken) && (outputToken == yToken)) || ((inputToken == yToken) && (outputToken == xToken)))
        {
            return ComputeType.Swap;
        } else if (((inputToken == xToken) || (inputToken == yToken)) && (outputToken == lpTokenId)) {
            return ComputeType.Deposit;
        } else if ((inputToken == lpTokenId) && ((outputToken == xToken) || (outputToken == yToken))) {
            return ComputeType.Withdraw;
        } else {
            revert INVALID_COMPUTE_TYPE();
        }
    }
```

But when the xToken or yToken in the pool is lpToken, then the function cannot enter the branch of the second `if` statement, and all Deposit operations will be recognized as Swap operations.

